  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Rain water has a&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pH</mi></math>&nbsp;of&nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;due to presence of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math>ions formed by the reaction of rain water with carbon dioxide present in the atmosphere.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8652;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#8652;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>HCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p>So, the correct option is A.</p>",
